zed; right operand is wrapped in `(` and `)` if and only if it is an operator node (`operator-node?` checks neither literal nor var).\n   - Faithful rendering: Left-leaning and right-leaning trees over the same leaves render differently (e.g. `1 * 2 + 3` vs `1 * (2 + 3)`).\n   - Round-trip fidelity: Parsed expressions produce left-leaning trees where the right child is always a leaf, rendering with zero parentheses and preserving tree equality across `(parse (render (parse s)))`.\n   - Shape validation: `render` calls `shapes/check! ::render e` at entry and passes the validated tree to `render*`. Non-conforming trees throw `ex-info` with `{:sandbox/error :invalid-expr ...}`.\n   - Single validation seam: Interior recursive calls use `render*` directly, ensuring `shapes/check!` is invoked exactly once at the entry seam.\n   - Dependencies: `sandbox.render` depends strictly on `sandbox.expr` and `sandbox.shapes`. No import or reference to `sandbox.parse` exists in the implementation.\n\n2. **Integration & Regression**:\n   - Existing property tests in `sandbox.property-test` (`parse-render-round-trips`, `canonical-is-idempotent`) continue to pass.\n   - Code formatting, linters, layer boundaries, and unit tests passed cleanly.\n\nNo findings. The diff satisfies all contract requirements and property targets.", :model "google/gemini-3.8-flash-20260902"} {:baseline {:tests 21, :assertions 71, :failures 0, :errors 0}, :method "exact literal replacement, required to match exactly once, then clojure -M:test; original bytes restored after each", :event/kind :mutation, :against "src/sandbox/render.clj (coder-r2, contract version 2)", :note "eleven mutants over all seven targets, D15's set with the finds adapted to this implementation; the Tester wrote against version 2 before the retry, so its tests are the ones the retry had to satisfy", :green-after? true, :event/at-ms 1861706, :mutants [{:name "a literal renders with a prefix", :target 1, :find "(expr/literal? e) (str (:e